Thanks @DanerSharifi-FR and @boubast for the fix and the thorough tests. Here is what I changed during review:

- I rebased the branch on 3.x and squashed it into one commit.
- Closing the dropdown (Escape, blur) had the same stale-results problem as a selection, so the fix now tracks which search the loaded options belong to, instead of setting a flag after a selection. Both cases go through the same check when the dropdown opens.
- I removed the change that marked every load as a first load, because after a preload it made the first typed character send a request, so the default 3-character minimum no longer applied.
- After a test dependency update on 3.x, the mocked requests now have absolute URLs, so I updated the new tests to match.
